slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

doc{$title"A complete website" $description"Copy, customize, test and publish a complete SLML website."
  t.lead"Start with a working four-page website, then make it yours. The starter in examples/starter includes a home page, an about page, a contact form and its local preview destination."
  section{$id"start" $title"1. Copy and preview"
    "From a checkout of the SLML repository:"
    code"""
        cp -R examples/starter my-site
        slml my-site
        """
    "On Windows, copy the examples/starter folder in File Explorer and run the same slml command. SLML opens its own native browser. Keep that window open while editing. It reloads after each save; an invalid page shows an error with the file, line and a hint."
    code"""
        my-site/
          layout.slml     shared styles, site frame and service cards
          index.slml      home page and responsive service grid
          about.slml      studio story and process
          contact.slml    labeled fields and required-field validation
          preview.slml    local destination for the demo GET form
        """
  }
  section{$id"customize" $title"2. Make the layout yours"
    "Open `layout.slml`. Change the studio name, colors and menu once; every page imports this file with `use\"layout.slml\"`. The `site` component provides the frame, and `slot` receives the content of each page."
    code"""
        slml 0.2
        use"layout.slml"
        site{$title"About — My studio" $description"What we do and how we work."
          #"A useful, welcoming website."
          "Replace this with your own story."
        }
        """
    "Set the right language in the shared `meta` element. Each page supplies its own title and search description through the component parameters. Add images with `img{./photo.jpg \"A description of the photo\"}`. Put photo.jpg next to the page."
    "The service grid uses `grid{cols3 cw260 g16 …}`: up to three equal columns, fewer when the window is narrow. The menu uses a wrapping row, so links move to another line instead of disappearing on a phone."
  }
  section{$id"form" $title"3. Try the form, then connect a real endpoint"
    "Open Contact in the native browser. Send it empty first: the window should say which required field is missing and put the caret into it. Enter made-up details, select a service, write a message and tick the demo box. Sending should take you to the local preview page. The optional web adapter (slml serve my-site --web --open) behaves the same way."
    note{$title"What the demo does"
      "The starter uses GET so you can test navigation without a server or account. Values are visible in the URL. The destination does not read them, store them or send a message. Use made-up details only."
    }
    "For real messages, replace the form's `>target` with your HTTPS endpoint and add the flag `post`:"
    code"""
        form.card{>https://example.com/contact post g18
          in{n:name "Your name" req}
          in{n:email "Email address" k:email req}
          area{n:message "Message" req}
          send.action"Send message"
        }
        """
    "Use an endpoint you control or the address supplied by a form service; example.com is only a placeholder. The endpoint must accept URL-encoded POST data and return a confirmation or redirect. Replace the demo checkbox and explanatory copy with wording appropriate to your actual service. Test the full submission before publishing."
    "See [Forms](/forms.slml) for the available field types and validation rules."
  }
  section{$id"test" $title"4. Check the complete site"
    +{g8
      "Follow every menu link from every page, including the Services anchor."
      "Make the browser narrow: the menu should wrap and the services should form one column."
      "In the optional web adapter, use Tab, Shift+Tab and Enter to navigate links and fields without a mouse."
      "In the optional web adapter, try an empty form, an invalid email and a complete submission."
      "Save an invalid element name and confirm that the preview shows a useful error. Fix it and confirm that the page returns."
    }
    code"slml check my-site"
    "This checks every page and local link. A failed check exits with status 1. It does not contact external websites or verify that a form service accepts your data."
  }
  section{$id"publish" $title"5. Share the native site or export explicitly"
    "Share the my-site folder with its .slml pages, imports and assets. Its reader opens it with slml my-site. The native browser currently loads local sites; remote HTTP(S) navigation remains planned."
    "For an existing HTML web host, explicitly select the compatibility exporter:"
    code"slml build my-site -o public"
    "Upload the contents of `public/`, including `_slml/`, to your static web host. Your shared layout file is a library and does not become an extra page. The output contains HTML, CSS and bundled fonts, with no JavaScript."
    "See [Building a website](/sites.slml#publish) for hosting examples. Keep the source folder: edit the .slml files and rebuild whenever you update the site."
  }
  pager{$prev"/sites.slml" $prev-label"Building a website" $next"/cli.slml" $next-label"Command line"}
}
